      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/a183cd/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2012-08-25T20:15:33.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>So after looking through all the villain flavor text and cards, I've noticed that all the villains have very decent reasons for the heroes to fight them. Except for Plague Rat. He's one of my favorite villains don't get me wrong, but how did he catch the heroes attention? What has he really done to make them fight him? Plague Rat pretty much sticks to himself in the sewers, eating anyone that might wander to close. That sounds pretty awful but the occasional missing person in a place like Rook City isn't that important. What makes him so important the that Freedom Five have to take time from stopping aliens invade the earth, to stop him from eating the stray hobo?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:36:04.373Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
